02cc5d05 GsXCh2z1rK3AW6nbcc8nEQAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAA 108:82a7616e63686f727391da004f2f55736572732f736861776e7361666661727368617267682f576f726b73706163652f636170746e2f706b672f636f672f6f62736572766174696f6e5f67726170682e676f3a313a312d3338383a31ac616e737765724c656e677468d10d35 Package `cog` wraps a generic cgraph.Graph[common.HashType, COGNode] in ObservationGraph. Contract per exported surface: -  - - NewObservationGraph(g): pure constructor storing the pointer as-is; a nil graph is not validated and will panic later in any method that dereferences Graph. - - WriteDOT(w io.Writer): emits `strict digraph`/`->` when Traits().IsDirected, else `strict graph`/`--`. AdjacencyMap failure is wrapped as `adjacency map: %w`; VertexWithProperties errors are returned bare/unwrapped. All fmt.Fprintf write errors are discarded, so a failing writer still yields nil. Output is deterministic: vertices and targets sorted by HashType.Sum(), attribute keys sorted lexically. An empty graph still produces the opening and closing braces and returns nil. - - WriteToFile(ctx, path): ctx is accepted but unused. os.Create and WriteDOT errors are returned verbatim (no wrapping, no sentinels). File is truncated/created; close is deferred so close errors are swallowed. - - QueryWithDepth(ctx, wspace, prov, n, q, depth): returns ("", ad-hoc fmt.Errorf) when wspace is nil or the root node n is nil — plain string errors, no sentinel values for callers to match. `depth` is accepted but never used. Propagates the QueryProviderWrapper(prov) error unwrapped. Side effect: always writes `./graph.gv` relative to CWD and discards that error completely. Then walks DetailedDFS from n.GetHash(); the visitor returns (true, err) to abort on Fprintf or parent Vertex lookup failure, and those errors surface unwrapped with an empty string result. Missing `observation-answer` attributes are tolerated via safeReadAttr instead of erroring. Success returns the accumulated explanation text. - - MultiGraphQueryWithDepth(ctx, wspace, prov, items, q, depth): nil wspace returns ("", error). A nil or empty items slice is NOT an error — the loop never executes and it returns ("", nil). Entries whose Graph or Root is nil are silently skipped with no error and no logging. `depth` is unused. Per item it runs the wrapped provider query then AdjacencyMap, VertexWithProperties, Edges, Edge; any failure aborts immediately returning ("", err) unwrapped. Vertices dedupe by hash and edges dedupe by a direction-normalized hash pair, so the first graph seen wins and reverse-direction edges collapse into one entry. Results are sorted deterministically by nodeLocation (source then target for edges). Builder Fprintf errors are checked and returned though they effectively cannot occur. -  - Helper contracts: observationGraphNodeLabel falls back fmt.Stringer → filepath.Base(GetFilePath()) → `%T`, never empty unless the Stringer returns empty. observationGraphNodeType falls back to `%T` for non-ast.ASTNode values. observationGraphImportType honors an existing import_type attribute (mapping PackageDependency to the literal "dependency"), otherwise infers from path substrings (toolchain path plus /src/ → stdlib, /pkg/mod/ or /vendor/ → dependency) and defaults to LocalDependency, so an empty file path classifies as local. formatDOTAttrs/formatDOTEdgeAttrs return "" for nil or empty maps and otherwise emit sorted pairs with trailing-comma vs leading-comma styles. nodeLocation returns pos.String() only for an ast.ASTNode with non-nil position, else GetFilePath() which may be empty. All helpers assume a non-nil COGNode; a nil interface panics on the Get* calls.
